    "case_id": "621",
    "case_summary": "A 51-year-old Hispanic man with a medical history of anxiety presented with 3 days of low back pain. Social history included active tobacco, alcohol, and marijuana use. Family history included prostate cancer (father), melanoma (brother), and colon cancer (niece).\n\nVital signs: blood pressure 160/80 mm Hg. Physical findings: right lower-quadrant abdominal pain and right paraspinal tenderness.\n\n- Laboratory tests:     - Hyponatremia (129 mmol/L)    - Leukocytosis (13.0 × 10⁹/L)     - Urinalysis: 15 mg/dL ketones    - Total metanephrine: 246 pg/mL (high; normal ≤205)    - Normetanephrine: 246 pg/mL    - Estradiol: 246 pmol/L (high; normal <143)    - Normal levels: Morning cortisol, ACTH, aldosterone, renin, DHEA sulfate, testosterone, 17-hydroxyprogesterone    - Initial serum β-hCG: 691 IU/L (normal 0-5 IU/L), increased to 1860 IU/L on repeat    - AFP: undetectable- Imaging studies:    1. CT abdomen/pelvis:       Title: Initial abdominal CT       Description: Large 8.1 × 6.7 × 8.6 cm well-circumscribed right suprarenal retroperitoneal hemorrhagic mass-like density without active extravasation        2. MRI adrenal protocol:       Title: Adrenal MRI       Description: Right adrenal hemorrhagic mass measuring 9.9 × 9.0 × 6.8 cm with mass effect to the inferior vena cava and right kidney        3. Testicular ultrasound:       Description: No neoplasm identified        4. Chest CT:       Description: Numerous pulmonary nodules- Pathology:    - Poorly differentiated tumor composed of syncytial, intermediate in situ trophoblastic cells    - Immunostaining positive for AE1/AE3, CAM5.2, inhibin, β-hCG (strongly), Glypican-3 and PLAP (focally)    - Negative for CD30, CD117, AFP, OCT4, calretinin, synaptophysin, Melan-A, ERG, CAIX, PAX8, TTF-1, and S100    - Lymph nodes negative for malignancy",
    "frontier": [
      "B1",
      "B2",
      "B3",
      "B4"
    ],
